    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "calling it 'conservative' feels like a bit of a cop-out to avoid the actual point though. even if definitions evolve, doesn't a standard of quality actually matter? if anyone can just slap some political text on a canvas and call it 'revolutionary' art, doesn't that just devalue the decades of work people put into mastering technique? it seems like the 'evolution' you're talking about is just a convenient excuse for people to ignore the fact that most contemporary art isn't actually good anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
